    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's definitely much more raw and captures that brutal atmosphere I was aiming for. It really highlights the danger Ezekiel is in.\n\nTo round out this scene, I want to show the psychological impact of this kind of rhetoric. Could you write a short internal monologue for Ezekiel right after the sheriff walks away? I want to see how he processes being spoken to that way—the anger, the need to stay composed for the sake of his community, and that feeling of being dehumanized by the very person meant to uphold the law. Just keep it in that same gritty, historical tone.",
